{"card_id":"puccini-tangram-small-palette","manual_id":"nl-amsterdam-puccini-method","pdf_id":"pdf-puccini-red-2021","title":"少量標準構件，多種街道組合","card_type":"design_principle","summary":"把鋪面、緣石、排水、家具與斷面原則整理成有限且相容的標準構件，再依街道情境組合，而不是每個專案重新發明一套材料語言。","application":"先建立可維護的構件庫與相容規則，再用基地條件決定組合；標準化不取代場地設計與專業判斷。","contexts":["urban_core","main_street","residential","neighbourhood"],"topics":["materials","cross_section","maintenance"],"elements":["street_material_palette","street_cross_section"],"source":{"section":"3.1 Tangramprincipe","page":"25","pdf_page":25},"translation_status":"agent_translated","version_warning":"來源為 2021 版；使用前須核對 Amsterdam 2024 現行手冊。","review":{"status":"source_checked","confidence":"high","professional_review_required":true}}
{"card_id":"puccini-simplicity-self-evidence","manual_id":"nl-amsterdam-puccini-method","pdf_id":"pdf-puccini-green-2021","title":"讓公共空間簡明且能被直覺理解","card_type":"design_principle","summary":"街道系統應以一致、克制而可辨識的空間語言，讓不同使用者容易理解路徑、邊界、優先次序與公共空間的用法。","application":"檢查同一功能是否使用一致構件、視覺訊息是否過量，以及無需額外標誌時空間本身能否傳達行為預期。","contexts":["urban_core","main_street","residential","shared_space","neighbourhood"],"topics":["materials","accessibility","road_safety"],"elements":["street_material_palette"],"source":{"section":"Overtuigingen","page":"13-15","pdf_page":15},"translation_status":"agent_translated","version_warning":"來源為 2021 版；使用前須核對 Amsterdam 2024 現行手冊。","review":{"status":"source_checked","confidence":"medium","professional_review_required":true}}
{"card_id":"puccini-craft-every-scale","manual_id":"nl-amsterdam-puccini-method","pdf_id":"pdf-puccini-green-2021","title":"從城市系統到收邊細節都維持工藝品質","card_type":"quality_method","summary":"公共空間品質同時取決於城市尺度的連續性、街道斷面的協調，以及緣石、樹穴、接縫和排水等細部的精確整合。","application":"設計審查同時檢查網路、斷面與細節三個尺度，避免整體概念正確但施工節點破壞無障礙、排水或景觀一致性。","contexts":["urban_core","main_street","residential","neighbourhood"],"topics":["materials","maintenance","accessibility","drainage"],"elements":["street_material_palette","street_cross_section"],"source":{"section":"Overtuigingen","page":"13-15","pdf_page":15},"translation_status":"agent_translated","version_warning":"來源為 2021 版；使用前須核對 Amsterdam 2024 現行手冊。","review":{"status":"source_checked","confidence":"medium","professional_review_required":true}}
{"card_id":"puccini-maintainability-early","manual_id":"nl-amsterdam-puccini-method","pdf_id":"pdf-puccini-green-2021","title":"把維護者帶進前期設計","card_type":"lifecycle_method","summary":"永續不只看初期材料或植栽效果，也包括可維護性、耐久性與全生命週期資源；管理維護單位應在早期參與。","application":"概念設計階段即確認清掃設備、樹木養護、排水清理、材料替換與交通維持需求，並把維護空間納入斷面。","contexts":["urban_core","main_street","residential","neighbourhood"],"topics":["maintenance","materials","green_infrastructure","drainage"],"elements":["street_material_palette","street_cross_section"],"source":{"section":"Overtuigingen","page":"13-15","pdf_page":15},"translation_status":"agent_translated","version_warning":"來源為 2021 版；使用前須核對 Amsterdam 2024 現行手冊。","review":{"status":"source_checked","confidence":"high","professional_review_required":true}}
{"card_id":"puccini-evidence-pilot-loop","manual_id":"nl-amsterdam-puccini-method","pdf_id":"pdf-puccini-green-2021","title":"以標準做基線，以試辦更新標準","card_type":"innovation_method","summary":"以已驗證的最佳實務保持城市品質，同時讓新方案透過小規模試辦、監測、評估和逐步納入標準，而不是一次全面導入。","application":"為偏離標準的創新提出假設、試辦範圍、成功指標、維護責任與停止條件；評估後決定擴大、修正或撤回。","contexts":["urban_core","main_street","residential","school","neighbourhood"],"topics":["tactical_urbanism","maintenance","engagement"],"elements":["engagement_process"],"source":{"section":"Overtuigingen","page":"13-15","pdf_page":15},"translation_status":"agent_translated","version_warning":"來源為 2021 版；使用前須核對 Amsterdam 2024 現行手冊。","review":{"status":"source_checked","confidence":"medium","professional_review_required":true}}
{"card_id":"puccini-whole-lifecycle-collaboration","manual_id":"nl-amsterdam-puccini-method","pdf_id":"pdf-puccini-green-2021","title":"設計、施工、驗收與管理是一條連續流程","card_type":"lifecycle_method","summary":"公共空間的品質需要設計、準備、執行、後續照護和日常管理之間的資訊連續與共同責任。","application":"建立每階段的交付物、決策責任與回饋節點；竣工後把實際材料、樹木、排水與維護需求回寫到資產資料。","contexts":["urban_core","main_street","residential","neighbourhood","network"],"topics":["maintenance","engagement","materials"],"elements":["engagement_process","street_material_palette"],"source":{"section":"Proces","page":"21-22","pdf_page":21},"translation_status":"agent_translated","version_warning":"來源為 2021 版；使用前須核對 Amsterdam 2024 現行手冊。","review":{"status":"source_checked","confidence":"high","professional_review_required":true}}
{"card_id":"kids-three-outcomes","manual_id":"int-gdci-designing-streets-for-kids","pdf_id":"pdf-gdci-kids-2020","title":"用三組兒童導向成果檢查街道","card_type":"evaluation_framework","summary":"兒童友善街道應同時安全健康、舒適便利，並具有啟發與教育價值；僅降低事故風險仍不足以形成可日常使用的好街道。","application":"每個替代方案都以三組成果列出設計回應、可量測指標與未解風險，避免只以車流效率或單一安全指標決策。","contexts":["school","residential","neighbourhood","network"],"topics":["school_streets","road_safety","accessibility","engagement"],"elements":["street_cross_section"],"source":{"section":"Why design streets for kids?","page":"5","pdf_page":23},"translation_status":"agent_translated","version_warning":null,"review":{"status":"source_checked","confidence":"high","professional_review_required":true}}
{"card_id":"kids-child-height-audit","manual_id":"int-gdci-designing-streets-for-kids","pdf_id":"pdf-gdci-kids-2020","title":"以兒童高度重新進行視線與體感稽核","card_type":"site_audit","summary":"幼兒身高與視點遠低於成人，停車、植栽、家具和路緣附近的遮蔽，會改變他們看見來車及被駕駛看見的能力。","application":"現勘與模型至少加入約 0.95 公尺高的三歲兒童視點，檢查穿越點、轉角、接送區與停車列的可視性；不可用成人視點替代。","contexts":["school","residential","neighbourhood"],"topics":["school_streets","road_safety","accessibility"],"elements":["street_cross_section"],"source":{"section":"Designing for kids","page":"11","pdf_page":29},"translation_status":"agent_translated","version_warning":null,"review":{"status":"source_checked","confidence":"high","professional_review_required":true}}
{"card_id":"kids-caregiver-pause-network","manual_id":"int-gdci-designing-streets-for-kids","pdf_id":"pdf-gdci-kids-2020","title":"把照顧者需求與可停留點納入路網","card_type":"design_method","summary":"兒童移動常由照顧者陪伴，且速度、載物、嬰兒車、休息、如廁與等候需求不同；路線品質取決於連續且可停留的整體旅程。","application":"沿主要兒童路線標記遮蔭、座椅、飲水、廁所、嬰兒車轉向與安全等候點，並檢查其間距、連續性及照護者視線。","contexts":["school","residential","neighbourhood","network"],"topics":["school_streets","pedestrian","accessibility","trees_public_realm"],"elements":["bikeway_network","sidewalk"],"source":{"section":"Designing for kids and caregivers","page":"11-19","pdf_page":29},"translation_status":"agent_translated","version_warning":null,"review":{"status":"source_checked","confidence":"medium","professional_review_required":true}}
{"card_id":"kids-engagement-toolkit","manual_id":"int-gdci-designing-streets-for-kids","pdf_id":"pdf-gdci-kids-2020","title":"讓兒童用多種媒介表達街道經驗","card_type":"engagement_method","summary":"兒童參與可透過地圖、日誌、繪畫與遊戲、街道稽核、照片故事、兒童帶路、觀察與計數等方法，不應只依賴成人式會議或問卷。","application":"依年齡、語言與能力組合至少兩種表達工具，保留兒童原始觀察，再由設計團隊說明哪些意見如何影響方案。","contexts":["school","residential","neighbourhood"],"topics":["engagement","school_streets"],"elements":["engagement_process"],"source":{"section":"Engaging kids","page":"142","pdf_page":160},"translation_status":"agent_translated","version_warning":null,"review":{"status":"source_checked","confidence":"high","professional_review_required":true}}
{"card_id":"everyday-inclusive-beyond-access","manual_id":"uk-everyday-streets-2023","pdf_id":"pdf-everyday-streets-2023","title":"把包容性從無障礙擴展到社會與經濟可及性","card_type":"evaluation_framework","summary":"街道包容性不只關乎坡度與淨寬，也涉及誰能停留、交易、工作、被看見、表達需求，以及誰因費用、管理或社會規範而被排除。","application":"在無障礙檢核之外，增加使用者群、活動時段、非正式經濟、管理規則、可負擔性與被排除經驗的盤點。","contexts":["urban_core","main_street","residential","shared_space","neighbourhood"],"topics":["accessibility","engagement","trees_public_realm"],"elements":["engagement_process","street_cross_section"],"source":{"section":"Introduction","page":"1-18","pdf_page":27},"translation_status":"agent_translated","version_warning":"書中文字採 CC BY-NC 4.0；第三方圖像權利另計。","review":{"status":"source_checked","confidence":"medium","professional_review_required":true}}
{"card_id":"everyday-localography","manual_id":"uk-everyday-streets-2023","pdf_id":"pdf-everyday-streets-2023","title":"用地方誌式研究理解感官、文化與日常行為","card_type":"site_research","summary":"Localography 是針對特定基地與脈絡的多媒介研究：結合聲音、視覺、氣味與觸覺，以及訪談、觀察、繪圖、步行和參與式行動。","application":"在幾何測量之外安排多時段步行與傾聽，建立感官地圖、行為記錄與地方敘事，作為斷面與營運方案的同等證據。","contexts":["urban_core","main_street","residential","shared_space","neighbourhood"],"topics":["engagement","trees_public_realm"],"elements":["engagement_process"],"source":{"section":"Localography","page":"241","pdf_page":267},"translation_status":"agent_translated","version_warning":"書中文字採 CC BY-NC 4.0；第三方圖像權利另計。","review":{"status":"source_checked","confidence":"high","professional_review_required":true}}
{"card_id":"everyday-co-drawing-protocol","manual_id":"uk-everyday-streets-2023","pdf_id":"pdf-everyday-streets-2023","title":"用共同繪圖平衡專業圖面與生活經驗","card_type":"engagement_method","summary":"共同繪圖需要一張可理解的底圖、明確但不封閉的操作規則，以及能促成對話的活動；其目的不是裝飾意見，而是讓生活經驗進入空間決策。","application":"準備比例適當的底圖和具體提示，依參與者調整圖例與工具；在早期及方案迭代時重複進行，並記錄設計回應。","contexts":["urban_core","main_street","residential","school","neighbourhood"],"topics":["engagement"],"elements":["engagement_process","street_cross_section"],"source":{"section":"Co-drawing","page":"274-278","pdf_page":300},"translation_status":"agent_translated","version_warning":"書中文字採 CC BY-NC 4.0；第三方圖像權利另計。","review":{"status":"source_checked","confidence":"high","professional_review_required":true}}
{"card_id":"everyday-street-inventory","manual_id":"uk-everyday-streets-2023","pdf_id":"pdf-everyday-streets-2023","title":"建立包含時間與感官的街道清冊","card_type":"site_audit","summary":"街道清冊不是一次拍照或只列硬體，而是以持續觀察、文件化與再現，記錄物件、活動、聲音、氣味、節奏及不同時段的變化。","application":"以固定觀察點和時間切片記錄空間、使用者、活動、停留與衝突，保留照片以外的聲音、註記與序列資料。","contexts":["urban_core","main_street","residential","shared_space","neighbourhood"],"topics":["engagement","maintenance"],"elements":["engagement_process","street_cross_section"],"source":{"section":"Street inventory","page":"279-283","pdf_page":305},"translation_status":"agent_translated","version_warning":"書中文字採 CC BY-NC 4.0；第三方圖像權利另計。","review":{"status":"source_checked","confidence":"high","professional_review_required":true}}
{"card_id":"tw18-walk-bike-integration-flow","manual_id":"tw-human-centered-urban-road-manual-2","pdf_id":"pdf-tw-human-road-2018","title":"先判斷人行與自行車是否應整合或分離","card_type":"selection_method","summary":"以道路條件、行人與自行車需求及可用空間逐步選擇共用、分流或其他配置，而不是預設把自行車放上人行空間。","application":"把流程當成初篩；最終斷面仍須依 2025 自行車手冊、2026 都市道路規範、流量、速度與無障礙需求檢核。","contexts":["urban_core","main_street","residential","school","neighbourhood"],"topics":["pedestrian","cycling","cross_section","accessibility"],"elements":["shared_use_path","bicycle_lane","sidewalk"],"source":{"section":"4.3 人行道與自行車道整合","page":"4-16","pdf_page":87},"translation_status":"original","version_warning":"2018 歷史手冊；不可作為 2026 年現行法規尺寸依據。","review":{"status":"source_checked","confidence":"high","professional_review_required":true}}
{"card_id":"tw18-road-space-redistribution","manual_id":"tw-human-centered-urban-road-manual-2","pdf_id":"pdf-tw-human-road-2018","title":"先檢討既有車行空間，再處理人行與自行車空間不足","card_type":"design_method","summary":"當人行或自行車空間不足時，應把車道數、車道寬、停車與路側使用納入重新分配，而不是只在既有邊角中擠入設施。","application":"建立現況與至少兩個重分配方案，量化每個方案的通行、停車、裝卸、轉彎、安全、樹木與排水影響。","contexts":["urban_core","main_street","residential","school","arterial","neighbourhood"],"topics":["cross_section","parking_curb","pedestrian","cycling"],"elements":["street_cross_section","motor_vehicle_lane","parking_bay"],"source":{"section":"4 人行空間","page":"4-1–4-16","pdf_page":72},"translation_status":"original","version_warning":"2018 歷史手冊；不可作為 2026 年現行法規尺寸依據。","review":{"status":"source_checked","confidence":"medium","professional_review_required":true}}
{"card_id":"tw18-bus-stop-bike-integration","manual_id":"tw-human-centered-urban-road-manual-2","pdf_id":"pdf-tw-human-road-2018","title":"公車站、自行車與候車空間需整體設計","card_type":"design_method","summary":"公車停靠、候車、上下車與自行車通行會在同一街道節點交織，必須共同處理動線、視線、無障礙與衝突，而非逐項疊加。","application":"以平面與時序圖檢查公車進出、乘客上下車、輪椅動線、候車排隊與自行車軌跡；明確標示優先順序和減速安排。","contexts":["urban_core","main_street","transit_corridor"],"topics":["transit","cycling","accessibility","road_safety"],"elements":["bicycle_lane","sidewalk"],"source":{"section":"9.3 公車候車亭與自行車道","page":"9-9","pdf_page":263},"translation_status":"original","version_warning":"2018 歷史手冊；節點尺寸與標線須依現行規範重查。","review":{"status":"source_checked","confidence":"high","professional_review_required":true}}
{"card_id":"tw25-bike-facility-selection","manual_id":"tw-bicycle-system-manual-2025","pdf_id":"pdf-tw-bike-2025","title":"以路網角色、速度、流量與空間選擇自行車設施","card_type":"selection_method","summary":"自行車設施型式應由路網功能、道路環境、車流與速度、使用者需求及可用空間共同決定，不宜只依道路等級或現有斷面選型。","application":"先定義目標使用者與路網連續性，再把各候選設施放入速度、流量、路側活動、路口及維護條件的比較矩陣。","contexts":["urban_core","main_street","residential","school","arterial","neighbourhood","network"],"topics":["cycling","road_safety","cross_section"],"elements":["bikeway_network","bicycle_lane","protected_cycle_track"],"source":{"section":"3.3 設施型式選擇","page":"3-9","pdf_page":31},"translation_status":"original","version_warning":null,"review":{"status":"source_checked","confidence":"high","professional_review_required":true}}
{"card_id":"tw25-riding-envelope-first","manual_id":"tw-bicycle-system-manual-2025","pdf_id":"pdf-tw-bike-2025","title":"先建立騎乘包絡與側向淨距，再談名目寬度","card_type":"geometry_method","summary":"自行車設施所需空間由車體、動態平衡寬度、側向淨距、使用者數與方向共同構成；標線到標線的名目寬度不能代表真正可騎寬度。","application":"斷面圖分別標示車體寬、動態寬、固定物與停車淨距、通行帶及不可騎區，再核對總寬。","contexts":["urban_core","main_street","residential","school","arterial","neighbourhood"],"topics":["cycling","geometric_design","cross_section"],"elements":["bicycle_lane","protected_cycle_track","buffer_zone"],"source":{"section":"4.2 寬度及淨空","page":"4-3","pdf_page":37},"translation_status":"original","version_warning":null,"review":{"status":"source_checked","confidence":"high","professional_review_required":true}}
{"card_id":"tw25-intersection-continuity","manual_id":"tw-bicycle-system-manual-2025","pdf_id":"pdf-tw-bike-2025","title":"自行車路線的安全取決於路口連續性","card_type":"intersection_method","summary":"自行車設施不應在路口前消失；穿越路徑、待轉或轉向、停等空間、視線及與行人和轉向車流的衝突都需在節點中清楚解決。","application":"逐一繪製各方向自行車軌跡、停等區、行人穿越及轉向車軌跡，找出衝突點並以幾何、號誌或時間分離處理。","contexts":["urban_core","main_street","residential","school","arterial","neighbourhood"],"topics":["cycling","intersections","road_safety"],"elements":["bicycle_lane","protected_cycle_track"],"source":{"section":"4.5 平面交叉","page":"4-15–4-18","pdf_page":49},"translation_status":"original","version_warning":null,"review":{"status":"source_checked","confidence":"high","professional_review_required":true}}
{"card_id":"nacto25-design-for-vulnerable-user","manual_id":"us-nacto-urban-bikeway-design-guide-3","pdf_id":"pdf-nacto-bike-2025","title":"以最脆弱的預期使用者控制設計","card_type":"design_principle","summary":"自行車設計的控制使用者應是最需要保護與空間的人，而不是只以最常見的小型自行車或最大汽車決定幾何。","application":"定義兒童、長者、適應型自行車、貨運自行車與大型微型移動裝置是否屬預期使用者，並據此檢查寬度、轉彎與操作空間。","contexts":["urban_core","main_street","residential","school","arterial","neighbourhood","network"],"topics":["cycling","accessibility","road_safety","geometric_design"],"elements":["bicycle_lane","protected_cycle_track","bikeway_network"],"source":{"section":"3.1 Designing Bikeways for All Ages & Abilities","page":"70-72","pdf_page":86},"translation_status":"agent_translated","version_warning":"NACTO 為專業指引，須與臺灣現行法規及道路條件並用。","review":{"status":"source_checked","confidence":"high","professional_review_required":true}}
{"card_id":"nacto25-rideable-width-not-painted-width","manual_id":"us-nacto-urban-bikeway-design-guide-3","pdf_id":"pdf-nacto-bike-2025","title":"可騎寬度要扣除害怕距離與不可騎表面","card_type":"geometry_method","summary":"可騎寬度是實際可操作的空間，不包含鄰近垂直物的避讓距離、排水溝槽或其他不可騎區；名目總寬不能直接當作能力指標。","application":"把設施畫成可騎帶、避讓帶、不可騎帶和維護淨寬四層，分別標註；審查時比較可騎寬而非只比較總寬。","contexts":["urban_core","main_street","residential","school","arterial","neighbourhood"],"topics":["cycling","geometric_design","maintenance"],"elements":["bicycle_lane","protected_cycle_track","buffer_zone"],"source":{"section":"Rideable Width","page":"73-74","pdf_page":89},"translation_status":"agent_translated","version_warning":"NACTO 為專業指引，須與臺灣現行法規及道路條件並用。","review":{"status":"source_checked","confidence":"high","professional_review_required":true}}
